<<tag character:Narrator>>
<<tag lore_id:lore_pipe_organ_glyph>>
Narrator: Above the pipe organ, gilded in flaking leaf, runs a single line of Tartarian script.
Narrator: The first phrase resolves into the modern tongue with effort: "Begin in the cellar of the chest."
Narrator: The second: "Earth at seven, heart at four-three-two, crown at five-two-eight."
Narrator: A resonance instruction. A trinity of tones — Telluric, Harmonic, Celestial — played from low to high.
Narrator: The third phrase is smudged with soot, as though someone has tried to erase it. Only one word survives: "doorway."
===
